  "summary": "Malicious code in modules-newline (npm)",
  "details": "The package declares a dependency on itself resolved from a non-registry plaintext HTTP host: dependencies and devDependencies both specify \"modules-newline\": \"hxxp://pack[.]nppacks[.]com/npm/modules-newline\". Installing this package redirects resolution of the modules-newline dependency away from the npm registry to an attacker-controlled HTTP server, which can serve arbitrary code in place of the package. The bundled code is a Babel plugin, but the dependency declaration is a supply-chain substitution vector.",
